ong.record-257rig-i4b"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257rig-i4b"],"id":"long.record-257rig-i4b","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Proposition 6.111 (A subpower bound for divisor counts)","locator":"Long record Proposition 6.111, p. 75, label record:257rig-i4b","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*For positive integers $n,k$, $\\tau(n)^k \\le (k^{2^k})^k\\cdot n$, or equivalently $\\tau(n)\\le k^{2^k}n^{1/k}$. The constant absorbs the finitely many primes below $2^k$; for larger primes, $(\\nu+1)^k\\le p^\\nu$ controls each factor of the divisor product. This estimate is independent of the support problem. The elementary zero-run bound above already follows from a single positive support element, without this estimate or a recurrence.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i4b","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i4b","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i4b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.card_divisors_le_divisorSubpowerConst_mul_rpow%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i4b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.card_divisors_le_divisorSubpowerConst_mul_rpow%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/lean.Erdos249257.card_divisors_le_divisorSubpowerConst_mul_rpow"},{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/nodes/long.record-257rig-i4b","id":"sha256:72b1b4c2b4a3766719310d7deb808e62432d8c1d3e4854b25b1285cbe6056696/edges/%5B%22long.record-257rig-i4b%22%2C%22lean.Erdos249257.card_diviso